WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Oh

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:06.319
At some point in our lives most of us have probably wished we could live forever

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:14.419
Being immortal sounds pretty good at first essentially not aging after a certain point being unable to die of natural causes not a bad life

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.219
But what if everyone became immortal overnight? What if the entire worlds population

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.849
stopped dying at the current rate approximately 150 to thousand people die every day around the world

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:28.130
That's about two per second

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:35.060
So assuming our immortality event happens instantly that would mean two unlucky souls would miss it by as little as a fraction of a second

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.139
If we assume everyone stopped dying at the time of making this video the world

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:42.500
population would quickly start climbing from about seven point six billion

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:49.999
At the current rate about three hundred sixty thousand people are born each day and the current death rate slows apparent population growth by about

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.270
42%

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:55.760
When this immortality event occurred we'd begin to see dramatic changes to our society

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.370
Contrary to what you'd probably expect

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:05.209
Overpopulation wouldn't be the first problem. We'd have to deal with if people stopped dying the population would start to increase more quickly

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.579
But it wouldn't become a crisis for at least a few years

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:13.279
one of the first negative impacts of this change would likely be the ironic death of the funeral industry if

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:17.629
No one dies of natural causes. There's no one to bury no funerals to arrange

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.109
No caskets to sell

00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:24.949
Funeral homes would have to rely on victims of violent crime car accidents and other unnatural causes of death to make a living

00:01:25.469 --> 00:01:33.199
Meanwhile in hospitals people sick with formerly terminal illnesses would exist in a permanent state of pain unable to die and their families would be

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:40.519
Stuck with their continued medical bills these hospitals would begin to become overcrowded as new patients are admitted for various unnatural injuries and conditions

00:01:41.039 --> 00:01:43.489
when the world begins to feel the strain of overpopulation

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:50.029
Especially after children are born grow up and start having children of their own. We'd begin to see crises in several areas

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:53.928
First natural resources would be depleted at an alarming rate

00:01:54.389 --> 00:02:00.859
Fossil fuels already running out today would be used up much more quickly forcing the world to adopt new sources of energy to keep society

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:02.130
running

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:07.759
Available land supply would dwindle with new housing springing up in any vacant lot to accommodate the rapidly growing population

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:13.609
Even if we could keep up with the demand for housing young people entering the job market would be met with little to no

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:20.149
Opportunity for employment all the jobs already snatched up by those who came before them as the unemployed begin to pile up

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:25.879
Homelessness would become a real problem made worse by the spike in housing prices when space inevitably runs out

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.840
Natural food would come at a premium as land used for livestock or crops

00:02:29.909 --> 00:02:33.138
Would dwindle and suffer under the strain of so many new mouths to feed

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:41.420
The food industry would have to turn to heavily processed and cheaply manufactured food potentially causing even more widespread nutritional problems than we have today

00:02:41.909 --> 00:02:48.259
With so many people out of work homeless and hungry and with no room to spread out civil unrest would start building

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.409
We'd begin to see riots in the streets of major cities anywhere

00:02:51.419 --> 00:02:57.859
There's a concentrated population of the unemployed on a larger scale nations without room for their citizens may feel the obligation

00:02:57.959 --> 00:03:02.179
To challenge their neighbors for their territory or resources sparking large Wars

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:10.459
governments would probably secretly see these Wars as serving multiple purposes to expand their territory and living space but also to help thin the

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:16.879
Population then there are more extreme possibilities with all other options exhausted perhaps we'd see a real-life

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.419
implementation of death sports like those in The Hunger Games or ancient Rome

00:03:20.519 --> 00:03:21.540
May be forced

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:27.679
Euthanasia would become the norm for the unfit both young and old in order to allow the healthiest members of society to survive

00:03:28.109 --> 00:03:35.059
Or more realistically we might see stringent restrictions on the number of children allowed per family perhaps based on social status

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:41.869
Occupation or income but if we could get the population growth under control the human race might not be as doomed as we think

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.339
We'd certainly have to live more frugal lives and likely have much less space to spread out

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:49.429
But with the right regulations in place it could be

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:54.470
Sustainable at least for the near future in the wake of our new immortality we might see new

00:03:54.569 --> 00:04:01.279
Technologies developed to accommodate the larger and longer lived population homes designed to allow humans to live in areas once considered undesirable

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:06.438
Allowing the more adventurous people to have a bit more space at the expense of safety or convenience

00:04:07.229 --> 00:04:14.299
Technological progress would likely increase as the demand for new innovations to help ease the population strain would grow and longer lives would allow

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:18.049
Scientists and innovators more time to perform studies and develop new ideas

00:04:18.539 --> 00:04:23.629
Provided the world didn't collapse beforehand on a personal level we might become more creative and artistic

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:29.179
our longer lives allowing us to pursue new hobbies and skills over decades instead of limiting ourselves to

00:04:29.409 --> 00:04:33.819
A few we'd have the chance to live smaller mini lives living in one place for 50 years

00:04:33.819 --> 00:04:38.889
Then moving and pursuing a new career somewhere else if the world could sustain such a drastic change

00:04:38.989 --> 00:04:43.299
It would be interesting to see what an immortal society would look like of course

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:49.479
It's very unlikely that it would as the strain from so many new mouths to feed and people to house would simply be too much

00:04:49.909 --> 00:04:54.819
Luckily immortality probably isn't something will ever have to accommodate and certainly not overnight

